Continuum is a hosted Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for
multi-agent coordination: a shared blackboard where agents write scoped
state, create and claim tasks, take advisory TTL locks, hand off work,
exchange inbox messages, and leave an append-only audit trail.

Continuum stores what happens next (execution state, minutes-to-hours).
For durable knowledge ("what is true"), pair it with the Heliofane
memory MCP; promote_to_memory bridges the two at handoff time.

Features:
- 22 MCP tools across blackboard, task, lock, context, agent presence,
  messaging, event log, status, and memory-promotion families
- Per-agent API-key authentication with full event attribution
- Three-engine storage: ValKey (ephemeral coordination), CouchDB
  (durable MVCC state + append-only event log), ArcadeDB (task
  dependency graph)
- Optimistic-concurrency claims (MVCC), advisory TTL locks, token-
  budgeted context packs with optional embedding-based ranking
- Read-only HTML dashboard and authenticated /metrics (Prometheus)
- Streamable HTTP + SSE transport at /mcp, plus a stdio transport
  for inspector debugging
